# Pull Before Push

Before every `git push` in this repository:

1. Confirm the working tree and current branch with `git status`.
2. Pull the latest version of that branch using rebase (for example, `git pull --rebase origin main`).
3. Resolve and verify any conflicts before pushing.
4. Push only after the pull/rebase succeeds.

Never skip the pull because the local tracking status appears current; fetch from the remote as part of the pull.
